  }))), "Project description"), mdx("p", null, "In this project, we build a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system for question answering on the HotpotQA dataset. Here we use an embedding model and FAISS to retrieve the most relevent chunks from a corpus built from HotpotQA. Then we send the question along with the retrieved chunks to an LLM to generate an answer."), mdx("p", null, "Here we compared three embedding models such as E5, BGE and GTE for retrieval quality, and we have also compared RAG vs non-RAG answers from the same LLM. We know that LLMs can sound very confident but still hallucinate the facts, especially on specific or multi-hop questions. For that we felt RAG is a common way to reduce this like instead of letting the model guess from memory, we give the LLMs real text from a knowledge source and ask it to answer based on that."), mdx("p", null, "Our main goal is generally to understand few things with a concrete dataset such as"), mdx("ul", null, mdx("li", {
